    "pressure": {
      "file": "cooling_tower_fan_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Fan lifts the air; the stack recovers velocity pressure",
      "description": "The induced-draught fan draws air through the louvres and fill, so the plenum below the fan is slightly below atmospheric pressure (typically ≈ 100–250 Pa of static pressure duty). Large fans turn slowly (tip speed usually ≤ ≈ 60 m/s for noise) and move very large volumes. The flared stack slows the leaving air, turning part of its velocity pressure back into static pressure, so the fan needs less power. Blade pitch is set to load the motor correctly; tip clearance to the stack should be small and even.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
  },
